«
@@ ============================================================
@@ MinTofDV — flight time minimising TrCost ΔV for a fixed departure date
@@ 1-D golden-section search; iteration count set by AstronTXPrecision
@@ (1 when the variable does not exist).
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@
@@ Input  : t₁ 'Af' 'Bf' tof_lo tof_hi   ( t₁ 'Af' 'Bf' tof_lo tof_hi -- { ΔV tof } )
@@ Output : { ΔV tof }
@@ The golden section reuses one point at each step and computes one new
@@ point, where a ternary search computed two. Its step count r is chosen
@@ so that the error bound, 0.618^r of the window, is at most that of the
@@ former ternary search of n = 3·AstronTXPrecision + 3 steps, which
@@ returned the middle of a final window of (2/3)^n: 9 TrCost instead of
@@ 13 at AstronTXPrecision 1.
@@ VALIDATION (simulator):
@@   1 'AstronTXPrecision' STO
@@   2459054 'Ⓛ♁Pf' 'Ⓛ♂Pf' 150 225 MinTofDV -> { 6.32099 205.66 }
@@ ============================================================
 → t1 Af Bf toflo tofhi
 «
   @ nstep = ⌈(n·ln 1.5 + ln 2) / ln(1/gold)⌉, n the former ternary step count
   IfErr 'AstronTXPrecision' Rcl Then Drop 1 End →Num 3 * 3 +
   1.5 Ln * 2 Ln + 0.6180339887498949 Inv Ln / Ceil
   toflo →Num tofhi →Num 0.6180339887498949
   → nstep lo hi gold
   «
     hi hi lo - gold * -  lo hi lo - gold * +
     → x1 x2
     «
       t1 t1 x1 + Af Bf ⓁTrCost 1 Get
       t1 t1 x2 + Af Bf ⓁTrCost 1 Get
       → f1 f2
       «
         1 nstep Start
           If f1 f2 < Then
             @ The minimum lies in [lo, x2]
             x2 'hi' Sto  x1 'x2' Sto  f1 'f2' Sto
             hi hi lo - gold * - 'x1' Sto
             t1 t1 x1 + Af Bf ⓁTrCost 1 Get 'f1' Sto
           Else
             @ The minimum lies in [x1, hi]
             x1 'lo' Sto  x2 'x1' Sto  f2 'f1' Sto
             lo hi lo - gold * + 'x2' Sto
             t1 t1 x2 + Af Bf ⓁTrCost 1 Get 'f2' Sto
           End
         Next
         If f1 f2 < Then f1 x1 Else f2 x2 End 2 →List
       »
     »
   »
 »
»
